# KHACHAPURI.JS — Crypto Pulse Conventions

House rules for the Crypto Pulse codebase. Every rule below exists for one of two reasons: it makes the auto-parsed sprint checkpoints pass, or it gives the mentor / jury something concrete to point at when scoring. When the course spec (`CODE_STANDARDS.md`, `SPRINT*_CHECKPOINT.md`) contradicts anything here, the course spec wins — please open a PR to update this file.

## A. Architecture & design

- **[A-01] Clean Architecture.** UI components handle display + user input only. Domain logic lives in services under `src/app/core/services/`. Components reach them via `inject()`.
- **[A-02] SOLID.**
  - **S** — one responsibility per class / function.
  - **O** — open for extension via abstract base + concrete impl (`LoggerService` → `ConsoleLoggerService`).
  - **L** — subclasses fully substitutable.
  - **I** — small, focused interfaces.
  - **D** — depend on abstractions through `InjectionToken` / `useExisting`, not concrete classes.
- **[A-03] KISS.** No premature abstraction. Prefer the simpler implementation.
- **[A-04] DRY.** Shared logic goes to `src/app/shared/utils/` or `src/app/core/services/`. Magic strings / numbers go to `src/app/core/constants/`.
- **[A-05] YAGNI.** Implement only what the current sprint checkpoint or mockup demands. Future-proofing is debt.
- **[A-06] Feature isolation.** `features/<name>/` must be self-contained. Cross-feature exports happen through `features/<name>/index.ts` barrels only.
- **[A-07] Layered imports.** `core` imports nothing. `shared` may import `core`. `features` may import `core` + `shared`. `layout` may import all. Never reverse.

## G. General

- **[G-01] TypeScript strict.** `strict: true` + `noImplicitOverride` + `noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature`. No `any`, no `as any`, no `@ts-ignore`. RxJS error params come in as `unknown` — narrow before use.
- **[G-02] File length.** Maximum 150 lines. If a component grows past that, split it or move logic into a service.
- **[G-03] Naming.**
  - Components: `PascalCaseComponent` (e.g. `WalletConnectModalComponent`)
  - Services: `PascalCaseService` (e.g. `WalletService`)
  - Pipes: `PascalCasePipe` (e.g. `PercentChangePipe`)
  - Directives: `PascalCaseDirective` (e.g. `PulseOnChangeDirective`)
  - Guards: `camelCaseGuard` (e.g. `walletConnectedGuard`)
  - Interceptors: `camelCaseInterceptor` (e.g. `loadingInterceptor`)
  - Folders & files: `kebab-case`
  - Injection tokens: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` (e.g. `WALLET_CONFIG`)
- **[G-04] Constants.** No hardcoded strings or numbers in components or services. Use `src/app/core/constants/*.constants.ts`.
- **[G-05] Logging & errors.**
  - HTTP errors are caught with `catchError` inside services and mapped to user-facing messages via `user-feedback.constants.ts`.
  - Global runtime errors go through `GlobalErrorHandler` → `LoggerService.error()` + `NotifierService.error()`.
  - Never call `console.*` directly anywhere. Use the `LoggerService` abstraction.
- **[G-06] Package manager.** Yarn only. Never `npm install` or `npm run`.
- **[G-07] Git discipline.** Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`, `test:`, `refactor:`, `ci:`). Branch names follow `feat/<scope>`, `fix/<scope>`. From Sprint 2 onward no direct push to `main` — everything via PR.
- **[G-08] Diary authenticity.** Files under `development-notes/<user>/` are written by hand in the contributor's own voice. Do not squash-merge diary commits — the parser checks commit dates against entry dates.

## O. Angular & performance

- **[O-01] Standalone only.** Every component / directive / pipe is `standalone: true` (Angular 21 default). No NgModules anywhere.
- **[O-02] OnPush everywhere.** `changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` is mandatory for every component, including pages.
- **[O-03] Signal-first state.**
  - Local state → `signal<T>(initial)`.
  - Derived state → `computed(() => ...)`. No side effects inside `computed`.
  - Side effects → `effect(() => ...)`. Use sparingly: persistence, logging, DOM-touching only.
  - State that derives from a signal but must remain independently writable → `linkedSignal(() => ...)`, not a `computed` + `effect` pair.
- **[O-04] Signal-based component API.** Use `input()`, `input.required()`, `output()`, `model()`. Never `@Input()` or `@Output()` decorators — they are listed as legacy in the course spec.
- **[O-05] New control flow.** Use `@if`, `@for`, `@switch`, `@defer` in templates. Never `*ngIf`, `*ngFor`, `*ngSwitch`. Every `@for` block must declare a `track` expression.
- **[O-06] `inject()` over constructor DI.** `private readonly svc = inject(SomeService)`. Constructors are reserved for `effect()` registration or non-DI logic.
- **[O-07] Singletons via `providedIn: 'root'`.** Services default to root unless explicitly feature-scoped via a `providers` array.
- **[O-08] Functional guards and interceptors.** Always functional (`CanActivateFn`, `CanDeactivateFn`, `HttpInterceptorFn`). Never class-based.
- **[O-09] Lazy loading.** Every route under the application shell uses `loadComponent` or `loadChildren`. The root `app.routes.ts` itself stays small and eager.
- **[O-10] RxJS boundary.** Streams live inside services. Components consume signals at the edge — convert via `toSignal()` or pipe into `signal.set` inside a `tap`. Manual subscriptions (rare) must use `takeUntilDestroyed()`.
- **[O-11] HTTP through services only.** Components never call `HttpClient` directly.
- **[O-12] Three-state UI.** Every async branch has explicit loading, empty, and error states. No blank flashes.

## F. Forms

- **[F-01] Reactive only.** `ReactiveFormsModule` + `NonNullableFormBuilder`. Template-driven forms are not used.
- **[F-02] At least two validators per field.** `required` plus at least one domain validator (`pattern`, `min`, `email`, or a custom `ValidatorFn`).
- **[F-03] Custom validators.** Pure `ValidatorFn` functions exported from `core/validators/` or a feature-local `validators/` folder.
- **[F-04] Inline error messages.** Displayed when `touched && invalid`. Message strings come from `core/constants/user-feedback.constants.ts`.

## T. Testing (Vitest)

- **[T-01] Collocation.** `*.spec.ts` lives next to the source file.
- **[T-02] Priority order.** Services > guards > pipes > directives > components. Cover the most logic-dense files first.
- **[T-03] HTTP tests.** Use `provideHttpClientTesting()` in `TestBed`. Mock services via `provide` + spy objects, not real instances.
- **[T-04] Naming.** `describe('WalletService', () => it('connects with mock provider after delay', ...))`. Sentence-case `it` strings.
- **[T-05] No tautologies.** Every `it` block must assert real observable behavior. No `expect(true).toBe(true)`.

## Q. Hygiene & quality

- **[Q-01] CI gate.** `yarn lint` + `yarn build` must pass on every push and PR. CI enforces.
- **[Q-02] No dead code.** No unused imports, vars, or exports. ESLint surface zero warnings.
- **[Q-03] Typed API.** Every HTTP response has an interface in `core/models/`. `unknown` exists only at the boundary, never bubbled into components.
- **[Q-04] Accessibility.** Semantic HTML + ARIA labels on interactive elements. Modals trap focus. Color contrast at WCAG AA.
- **[Q-05] Member visibility.**
  - `private readonly` for injected dependencies.
  - `protected` for members consumed by templates (Angular 21 idiom).
  - `public` only when something is genuinely part of the cross-feature surface.
- **[Q-06] Encapsulated signals.** Private writable: `private readonly _state = signal(...)`. Public read-only: `readonly state = this._state.asReadonly()`.
- **[Q-07] JSDoc on public APIs.** Service public methods plus non-obvious `computed` / `effect` blocks get a short JSDoc explaining intent. The mentor interview is easier when the reasoning is captured in code.

## I. CI & hosting

- **[I-01] GitHub Actions.** `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs on `push` and `pull_request` to `main`. Use the Node version from `.nvmrc`; gate with `yarn install --frozen-lockfile`, `yarn lint`, and `yarn build --configuration production` (same as [Q-01] locally).
- **[I-02] Vercel.** Root `vercel.json` pins `installCommand`, `buildCommand`, `outputDirectory` (`dist/crypto-pulse/browser`), and SPA `rewrites` so deep routes work after refresh.
- **[I-03] README deployment.** Keep the CI badge and a working **HTTPS** production link in README `Deployment` before Collaborator / checkpoint review.
- **[I-04] Shared Cursor rules.** `.gitignore` keeps ephemeral `.cursor/` noise out but **commits** `.cursor/rules/` so the team shares the same agent conventions.

## P. Project-specific (Crypto Pulse — wallet-mock path)

- **[P-01] No Binance API key.** Trading endpoints are simulated through `MockApiService` (`of(...).pipe(delay())`). No NestJS backend. The deviation is documented in README "Project Notes".
- **[P-02] Real public market data.** Prices come from Binance Spot Testnet public endpoints through `MarketDataService`. No auth header.
- **[P-03] Mock trading data.** Portfolio holdings, orders, deposits, withdrawals come from `MOCK_*` constants combined with simulated latency.
- **[P-04] `WalletService` is the centerpiece.** It demonstrates signals + computed + effect + RxJS + DI + persistence in one file. Use it as the reference when explaining the architecture.
- **[P-05] RS School logo.** Mandatory on the `/about` page (clickable, links to `https://rs.school`). Optional flair as an "RS Demo Wallet" entry in the wallet provider list, clearly marked as a course demo.
- **[P-06] Beyond-API trio.** Wallet connect (mock), price alerts, virtual deposit / withdraw. All three persist to `localStorage`.

